<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103152" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τερηδών</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όνος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wood-worm</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1308
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				5.4.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				6.10.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>a grub</i> which infests beehives, larva of the wax-moth,
				<i>Galleria mellonella</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυραύστης</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				605b17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>a worm in the bowels</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				241
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>caries</i>, in the bones, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Morb.</u>
				2.24
			</span></i>, al. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετραίνω</span>, Skt.
				<i>tṛṇatti</i> 'bore through', Lith.
				<i>trandis</i> 'hairworm, moth'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
